ta Format Expected by RSTIB:\n   - batch[\'X\']: shape [B, L, N, C] where:\n     * B: batch size\n     * L: input_window (12)\n     * N: number of nodes\n     * C: feature channels (1 + time_in_day + day_in_week)\n\n   Feature Channels Breakdown:\n   - Channel 0: Traffic speed/flow data (input_dim=1)\n   - Channel 1: Time in day (normalized 0-1, if add_time_in_day=true)\n   - Channel 2: Day in week (0-6, if add_day_in_week=true)\n\n   Compatible Datasets:\n   1. METR_LA\n      - Nodes: 207\n      - Features: speed only\n      - Temporal resolution: 5 minutes\n      - Recommended: YES (most commonly used)\n\n   2. PEMS_BAY\n      - Nodes: 325\n      - Features: speed + occupancy\n      - Temporal resolution: 5 minutes\n      - Recommended: YES (larger scale)\n\n   3. PEMSD3\n      - Nodes: 358\n      - Temporal resolution: 5 minutes\n      - Recommended: YES\n\n   4. PEMSD4\n      - Nodes: 307\n      - Temporal resolution: 5 minutes\n      - Recommended: YES\n\n   5. PEMSD7\n      - Nodes: 883\n      - Temporal resolution: 5 minutes\n      - Recommended: YES (comprehensive testing)\n\n   6. PEMSD7(M)\n      - Nodes: 228 (monthly)\n      - Temporal resolution: 5 minutes\n      - Recommended: MAYBE (shorter time window)\n\n   7. PEMSD8\n      - Nodes: 170\n      - Temporal resolution: 5 minutes\n      - Recommended: YES\n\n   8. LOOP_SEATTLE\n      - Nodes: 323\n      - Temporal resolution: 5 minutes\n      - Recommended: YES\n\n   9. T_DRIVE20150206\n      - Nodes: 12000+ taxi locations\n      - Recommended: YES (taxi trajectory data)\n\n   Dataset Compatibility: FULL PASS\n   - All standard LibCity traffic datasets work with TrafficStatePointDataset\n   - RSTIB properly handles temporal features\n   - No dataset-specific modifications required\n\n6. TEMPORAL FEATURE REQUIREMENTS\n\n   RSTIB requires temporal context for:\n   - Time-of-day embeddings (to capture rush hour patterns)\n   - Day-of-week embeddings (to capture weekly patterns)\n\n   LibCity Handling:\n   -