n```\nRuntimeError: Expected all tensors to be on the same device, but found at least two devices, cuda:0 and cpu!\n```\n\n**Location:** `RSTIB.py:245` in `reparametrize_n()` method\n\n**Root Cause:**\n```python\n# Line 244 in RSTIB.py\neps = Variable(cuda(std.data.new(std.size()).normal_(), std.is_cuda)).to(self.device)\n```\n\nThe `cuda()` helper function places tensor on CUDA when `std.is_cuda=True`, but the model is on CPU. The subsequent `.to(self.device)` doesn\'t fix this because the Variable is already created with mixed devices.\n\n**Diagnosis:**\n- The model parameters are on CPU (`device: cpu`)\n- Config specifies `device: cuda:0`\n- The `cuda()` function creates tensors on CUDA regardless of `self.device`\n- This creates a device mismatch\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```python\n# Replace line 244\neps = std.data.new(std.size()).normal_().to(self.device)\n```\n\nOr ensure model is moved to device after initialization:\n```python\nmodel = RSTIB(config, data_feature).to(config[\'device\'])\n```\n\n**Success on CPU:**\n- Forward pass works correctly on CPU\n- Output shape: `(B, output_window, N, output_dim)` = `(4, 12, 207, 1)` ✓\n- No NaN/Inf values ✓\n\n---\n\n### Test 4: Loss Calculation Test ✗ FAIL\n**Status:** FAILED  \n**Error:**\n```\nRuntimeError: The size of tensor a (12) must match the size of tensor b (4) at non-singleton dimension 1\n```\n\n**Location:** `RSTIB.py:406` in `calculate_loss()` method\n\n**Root Cause:**\n```python\n# Lines 406-407 - INCORRECT\ny_true_noisy = y_true_inv + noise_y.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)\ny_predicted_noisy = y_predicted_inv + noise_y.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)\n```\n\n**Shape Analysis:**\n- `y_true_inv`: `[B=4, T=12, N=207, D=1]`\n- `noise_y`: `[B=4, T=12, N=207, 1]`\n- `noise_y.squeeze(-1)`: `[B=4, T=12, N=207]`\n- `noise_y.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)`: `[B=4, N=207, T=12]` ❌ WRONG!\n\nThe transpose swaps the time and node dimensions, causing a shape mismatch.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```python\n# Lines 406-407 - CORRECTED\ny_true_noisy = y_true_inv + noise_y\ny_predicted_noisy = y_predicted_inv + noise_y\n```\n\n`noise_y` already has the correct shape `[B, T, N, 1]` to add to `y_true_inv` and `y_predicted_inv`.\n\n---\n\n### Test 5: Information Bottleneck Components Test ✗ FAIL\n**Status:** FAILED (due to device issue in Test 3)\n\n**Expected Outputs (from CPU test):**\n- `y_predicted`: `[4, 12, 207, 1]` ✓\n- `encoding`: `[4, 128, 207, 1]` ✓\n- `mu`: `[4, 128, 207, 1]` ✓\n- `std`: `[4, 128, 207, 1]` ✓\n- `noise_y`: `[4, 12, 207, 1]` ✓\n- `mu_y`: `[4, 12, 207, 1]` ✓\n- `std_y`: `[4, 12, 207, 1]` ✓\n- `mu_x`: `[4, 256, 207, 1]` ✓\n- `std_x`: `[4, 256, 207, 1]` ✓\n\nAll shapes are correct when running on CPU.\n\n---\n\n### Test 6: LibCity Full Training Test ✗ FAIL\n**Status:** FAILED  \n**Error:**\n```\nKeyError: \'0 is not in the batch\'\n```\n\n**Location:** `RSTIB.py:298` in `forward_ib()` method\n\n**Root Cause:**\n```python\n# Line 298 - INCORRECT\nif self.if_dne and \'te\' in batch:\n```\n\nThe `Batch` class in LibCity doesn\'t implement `__contains__` method. When Python checks `\'te\' in batch`, it treats the string \'te\' as an iterable and checks each character. The error `\'0 is not in the batch\'` occurs because Python is checking if \'t\' (index 0) is in the batch.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```python\n# Line 298 - CORRECTED\nif self.if_dne and hasattr(batch, \'data\') and \'te\' in batch.data:\n```\n\nOr add to Batch class:\n```python\ndef __contains__(self, key):\n    return key in self.data\n```\n\n---\n\n## Critical Bugs Summary\n\n### Bug #1: Device Placement in Reparameterization (CRITICAL)\n- **File:** `RSTIB.py`\n- **Line:** 244\n- **Impact:** Prevents training on GPU\n- **Fix:** Replace `Variable(cuda(...)).to(self.device)` with direct `.to(self.device)`\n\n### Bug #2: Noise Tensor Shape Mismatch (CRITICAL)\n- **File:** `RSTIB.py`\n- **Lines:** 406-407\n- **Impact:** Prevents loss calculation\n- **Fix:** Remove `.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)` - use `noise_y` directly\n\n### Bug #3: Batch Key Check (MEDIUM)\n- **File:** `RSTIB.py`\n- **Line:** 298\n- **Impact:** Runtime error when DNE is enabled\n- **Fix:** Use `hasattr(batch, \'data\') and \'te\' in batch.data`\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Fixes\n\n### Priority 1: Fix Loss Calculation (Bug #2)\n**Location:** `libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py:406-407`\n\n**Current Code:**\n```python\ny_true_noisy = y_true_inv + noise_y.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)\ny_predicted_noisy = y_predicted_inv + noise_y.squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)\n```\n\n**Fixed Code:**\n```python\ny_true_noisy = y_true_inv + noise_y\ny_predicted_noisy = y_predicted_inv + noise_y\n```\n\n### Priority 2: Fix Device Placement (Bug #1)\n**Location:** `libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py:244`\n\n**Current Code:**\n```python\neps = Variable(cuda(std.data.new(std.size()).normal_(), std.is_cuda)).to(self.device)\n```\n\n**Fixed Code:**\n```python\neps = std.data.new(std.size()).normal_().to(self.device)\n```\n\n### Priority 3: Fix Batch Key Check (Bug #3)\n**Location:** `libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py:298`\n\n**Current Code:**\n```python\nif self.if_dne and \'te\' in batch:\n```\n\n**Fixed Code:**\n```python\ntry:\n    if self.if_dne and \'te\' in batch.data:\n        dne = self.construct_dne(batch[\'te\'].type(torch.LongTensor))\n        node_emb.append(dne)\nexcept (KeyError, AttributeError):\n    pass\n```\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Verification ✓\n\nThe model architecture is correctly implemented:\n\n1. **Time Series Embedding Layer**: Conv2d(12, 64) ✓\n2. **Spatial Node Embeddings**: [207, 64] ✓\n3. **Temporal Embeddings**: \n   - Time in day: [288, 64] ✓\n   - Day in week: [7, 64] ✓\n4. **MLP Encoder**: 2 layers of [320, 320] ✓\n5. **Information Bottleneck Layers**:\n   - Encoding dimension K: 160 (hidden_dim // 2) ✓\n   - Output dimension reduction: Conv2d(160, 12) ✓\n   - Reconstruction dimension increase: Conv2d(160, 320) ✓\n6. **Regression Layer**: Conv2d(160, 12) ✓\n7. **Dynamic 