\'te\') if hasattr(batch, \'get\') else batch.data.get(\'te\', None) if hasattr(batch, \'data\') else None\n        if te is not None:\n            dne = self.construct_dne(te.type(torch.LongTensor).to(self.device))\n            node_emb.append(dne)\n        else:\n            # Add zero-padding to maintain dimension consistency\n            B = history_data.shape[0]\n            N = history_data.shape[2]\n            zero_dne = torch.zeros(B, self.node_dim, N, 1, device=self.device)\n            node_emb.append(zero_dne)\n            self._logger.debug("DNE feature unavailable, using zero padding")\n    except (KeyError, AttributeError) as e:\n        # Add zero-padding on error to maintain dimension consistency\n        B = history_data.shape[0]\n        N = history_data.shape[2]\n        zero_dne = torch.zeros(B, self.node_dim, N, 1, device=self.device)\n        node_emb.append(zero_dne)\n        self._logger.debug(f"DNE feature skipped: {e}, using zero padding")\n```\n\n## Key Improvements\n\n1. **Dimension Consistency**: Zero-padding ensures encoder always receives expected 320 channels\n2. **Graceful Degradation**: Handles missing \'te\' key without crashing\n3. **Architecture Consistency**: Maintains consistency between initialization and forward pass\n4. **Proper Device Placement**: Uses `device=self.device` for correct device handling\n5. **Informative Logging**: Logs when zero-padding is used for debugging\n\n## Testing\n\nA test script has been created to verify the fix:\n- Location: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/test_rstib_import.py`\n- Tests:\n  1. Model import\n  2. Model instantiation with `if_dne=True`\n  3. Forward pass with missing \'te\' key (simulates bug scenario)\n  4. Output shape verification\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nWhen `if_dne=True` but \'te\' key is missing:\n- **Before Fix**: RuntimeError with dimension mismatch (256 vs 320 channels)\n- **After Fix**: Zero-padding added, model processes normally with 320 channels\n- Log message: "DNE feature unavailable, using zero padding"\n\n## Impact\n\n- **Backward Compatible**: Works with both old and new batch formats\n- **No Performance Impact**: Zero-padding is computationally negligible\n- **Robust**: Handles edge cases gracefully\n- **Maintains Model Logic**: DNE functionality preserved when \'te\' is available\n'}
